## Notion Features → Dopaqueue Adaptation

| Notion Feature | What It Does | Dopaqueue Adaptation | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Multiple Views (List/Board/Gallery)** | See same data differently | **View Switcher:** Toggle between List View (compact, Todoist-style), Card/Gallery View (thumbnails, Pinterest-style), and Board View (Kanban by status) | v1 |
| **Properties/Metadata** | Custom fields on items | **Auto-Properties:** Platform, content type, domain, save date, tags, urgency — all auto-detected. User can add notes + timer | v1 |
| **Favorites / Pinned** | Quick access to important items | **Pinned Saves:** Long-press → "Pin to top." Pinned items always appear first | v1 |
| **Templates** | Reusable structures | **Save Templates:** "Research Mode" (auto-tag #research, assign to Research collection, set reminder for tomorrow). User creates presets for different save workflows | v2 |
| **Linked Databases** | Same items appear in multiple views | **Smart Collections:** A save can belong to multiple collections. A "Smart Collection" auto-populates based on filters (e.g., "All YouTube videos tagged #learn") | v2 |
| **Toggle Blocks** | Expand/collapse sections | **Collapsible Sections:** In collection view, sections collapse/expand cleanly | v1 |
| **Breadcrumb Navigation** | Know where you are in hierarchy | **Breadcrumb Bar:** Inbox > Collections > Focus > Item Detail | v1 |
| **Page Content** | Rich text editor inside each page | **Save Detail Page:** Open a save to see full metadata, thumbnail, notes, link, tags — but NOT a full rich text editor (keep it simple) | v1 |
| **Cover Images** | Visual headers | **Collection Covers:** Collections show the thumbnail of the first item as a cover image, or user picks one | v2 |
| **Databases** | Structured tables | Too complex — skip. Our views (list/board/gallery) cover this without the complexity | — |

