## The "Migration Magnet" Features

These are the specific features that make users of basic apps think *"I need to switch to Dopaqueue"*:

### From Notes Apps (Google Keep, Apple Notes)
> **What they lack:** No link preview, no auto-metadata, no platform detection, no media handling
> **Dopaqueue wins with:** Automatic rich link previews, thumbnail extraction, platform badges, and the Share Intent save flow

### From Todoist
> **What it lacks:** Todoist is terrible at saving links/media. It treats URLs as plain text with no preview
> **Dopaqueue wins with:** First-class link/media handling + Todoist-level organization (priorities, due dates, projects)

### From Notion
> **What it lacks:** Notion is painfully slow on mobile, requires too many taps to save something, and has no Share Intent integration
> **Dopaqueue wins with:** 1-tap saving, instant offline performance, and the same organizational power in a fraction of the complexity

### From Pocket/Raindrop
> **What they lack:** No task management, no reminders, no urgency levels, no "process your saves" workflow
> **Dopaqueue wins with:** Inbox Zero flow, save timers, urgency flags, and the swipe-to-process UX

